  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.5: Documentation and hardening update — the library binary is identical to 1.0.0-preview.3 (no code change; supersedes the unpublished preview.4 tag). Reworded the API-stability language (the public API/wire format are stable across the preview series; the preview suffix reflects the pending independent audit, not API churn). Clarified JOSE/IANA standards status (ML-DSA-65 and A256GCM are registered JOSE identifiers per RFC 9964 / RFC 7518, but the X-Wing key-management profile is not a standardized JOSE/JWE profile), added a normative v1 token profile (docs/SPEC.md), expanded the security model, strengthened production-readiness guidance, clarified replay-protection/key-rotation posture, made hybrid wording precise (hybrid confidentiality, ML-DSA-65 signatures), and aligned package positioning for controlled issuer/verifier systems. Production-oriented preview: NOT independently audited, NOT a drop-in OAuth/OIDC/JWT replacement. Full notes: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md — known limitations: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/KNOWN-GAPS.md.",
